-- title:
--   Level-ℓ fine uniformisation depends only on Frobenius-fixed coefficients
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the standard frame for the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of a quaternionic Shimura curve, and the hypotheses are grouped as follows.
--
--   **Numerical data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a nonzero natural number $N$ with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree.
--
--   **The $r$-adic base.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $\pi$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue field of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The unramified layer.** A characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: $\pi$-adic completeness (`hOnr_complete`), maximality of the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_max`), integrality of every element modulo $\pi$ in the sense that each $x$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ whose value at $x$ lies in $(\pi)$ (`hOnr_alg`), existence modulo $\pi$ of a root of every monic polynomial of positive degree (`hOnr_closed`), and the congruence $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **The determinant valuation.** A monoid homomorphism $v_{\det} \colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $v_{\det}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The indefinite algebra and its coarse moduli scheme.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $r \in v$ or $\bar r \in v$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`: an order not properly contained in any order). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, a point assignment `pt` sending each fake elliptic curve of level $N$ over an $\mathcal O$-algebra $S$ to an $S$-point of $\mathcal X$ over the base, and `h𝒳 : IsCoarseModuli`, whose five clauses require invariance of `pt` under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback along ring maps, surjectivity and injectivity of `pt` up to isomorphism on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property of a coarse moduli scheme. Two typeclass hypotheses state that the second projection of the pullback of $f$ along $\operatorname{Spec}(K_0) \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O)$ is geometrically reduced (`hgr`) and geometrically connected (`hgc`).
--
--   **Auxiliary full level and the twisting group.** A natural number $n \ge 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $n$ coprime to $N$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ via $f_M$, a point assignment `ptF` on fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure, and `hM : IsFineModuli` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, and bijectivity of `ptF` up to isomorphism over every $\mathcal O$-algebra). A group $G$ with $\rho \colon G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ and $\chi \colon G \to \Lambda$, and `hρ : IsLevelTwistAction`, whose clauses require that each $\rho(h)$ lies over the base, that $\rho(h)$ realises the twist of the level structure by $\chi(h)$, and that $\chi$ is multiplicative, unital, surjective and injective modulo $n\Lambda$.
--
--   **Comparison of the two moduli problems.** A morphism $p \colon M \to \mathcal X$ with $p$ followed by $f$ equal to $f_M$ (`hp`), invariance of $p$ under the $G$-action (`hρp`), and compatibility of $p$ with the two point assignments (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **The Hecke tower.** For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ via $g_\ell$, a point assignment `ptT` on fake elliptic curves with extra level $\ell$, and `h𝒴 : IsCoarseModuliT` (the analogue of the coarse moduli conditions for the extra-level functor). Degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1 \colon \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ lying over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`), with `hd₀` stating that $d_0$ forgets the extra level and `hd₁` that $d_1$ sends a point of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ to the point of the target of any level-$\ell$ isogeny out of it.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner data.** Morphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r} \colon \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`), compatible with `pt` through the relation `FakeEllipticCurve.IsAtkinLehnerQuotient` at $r$ and at $\bar r$ respectively (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$, and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $\bar r \in v$. A maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) with $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$, an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$, and `hS₁`: $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$. An injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0 \colon \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$, and a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$.
--
--   **The discrete group and the tower elements.** A subgroup $\tilde\Gamma$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ whose elements are exactly those of [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37) (`hΓt`). For each tower prime $\ell$, a global unit $s_\ell$ and an adelic unit $sf_\ell$ with `hs`: $sf_\ell$ is the image of $s_\ell$ at every place not containing $r$, is $1$ at every place containing $r$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; and $\tilde\Gamma(\ell) = \tilde\Gamma \cap s_\ell \tilde\Gamma s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w) = \bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`). A group homomorphism $\theta_t \colon \tilde\Gamma \to G$.
--
--   **The uniformisation families.** For every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map $\Theta_f$ from $\bigl(\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(O^{\mathrm{nr}},B) \times \hat\Omega(B)\bigr) \times G$ to the set of $B$-points of $M$ over $\mathcal O$, where $\hat\Omega(B)$ is the value at $B$ of `Omega K₀ π`, the set of Deligne data: assignments to each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M \subset K_0^2$ of a $B$-submodule of the base change with invertible quotient, monotone under inclusions of lattices, equivariant for scalar homotheties, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$. Similarly, for each tower prime $\ell$ a map $\Theta_T$ into the $B$-points of $\mathcal Y_\ell$, without the $G$-factor. The family $\Theta_f$ satisfies: `hnat`, naturality in $B$ along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; `hG`, that composing $\Theta_f(x, g h)$ with the automorphism $\rho(h)$ gives $\Theta_f(x,g)$; `hinv`, that for $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma$ and points $x, x'$ related by `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\iota_0(\gamma)$ — that is, the coefficient leg of $x'$ is that of $x$ precomposed with $\mathrm{Fr}^{-v_{\det}(\iota_0\gamma)}$, and the $\hat\Omega$-leg of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ — one has $\Theta_f(x', \theta_t(\gamma) g) = \Theta_f(x,g)$; and `het`, a unique-lifting property: for every surjection $p \colon B \to B_0$ of $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent in both and with the product of any two elements of $\ker p$ zero, and every $x_0$ over $B_0$ and $B$-point $y$ of $M$ whose image is $\Theta_f(x_0)$, there is a unique $x$ over $B$ with image $x_0$ and $\Theta_f(x) = y$.
--
--   **The level-$\ell$ datum.** A tower prime $\ell$, a scheme $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ via $f_{M_\ell}$ with $f_{M_\ell}$ locally of finite type (`hfMℓ`), and a family $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ from $\bigl(\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(O^{\mathrm{nr}},B) \times \hat\Omega(B)\bigr) \times G$ to the $B$-points of $M_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$, natural in $B$ (`hnatℓ`) and satisfying the twisted invariance `hinvℓ` for those $\gamma$ which lie both in $\tilde\Gamma$ and in $\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$: if $x,x'$ are related by `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\iota_0(\gamma)$, then $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x', \theta_t(\gamma) g) = \Theta_{f,\ell}(x,g)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, every pair of $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\psi, \psi' \colon O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, every Deligne datum $P \in \hat\Omega(B)$ and every $g \in G$: if $\psi(y) = \psi'(y)$ holds for every $y \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with the property that $\mathrm{Fr}^{\,v_{\det}(\iota_0 z)}(y) = y$ for all $z \in \tilde\Gamma$ which are rational scalars (i.e. $z = c \cdot 1$ for some $c \in \mathbb Q$) and satisfy $\theta_t(z) = 1$, then
--   $$\Theta_{f,\ell}\bigl((\psi, P), g\bigr) = \Theta_{f,\ell}\bigl((\psi', P), g\bigr).$$
--   That is, the level-$\ell$ family depends on its coefficient leg only through the restriction of that leg to the subring of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ fixed by all the Frobenius powers attached to the central elements of $\tilde\Gamma$ in the kernel of $\theta_t$.
--
--   This is the coefficient-invariance step for the level-$\ell$ layer of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the quaternionic moduli tower: the uniformising family over the formal upper half plane, evaluated at a level-$\ell$ scheme, is unchanged when the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-coefficient map is altered outside the subring fixed by the Frobenius powers coming from central elements of $\tilde\Gamma$ killed by $\theta_t$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.exists_apply_ne_zero_forall_isPullback_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.exists_apply_ne_zero_forall_isPullback_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine_eq) to produce points of the level-$\ell$ scheme with prescribed pullback behaviour.
